From: programista-zacny <5969291+programista-zacny@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] bcmdhd4358a3: optional cfg80211 scheduled scan for PNO

Android's Wi-Fi framework reconnects with the screen off through PNO:
WifiConnectivityManager asks WifiScanningService, which asks wificond,
which sends NL80211_CMD_START_SCHED_SCAN. This driver has a complete
scheduled-scan implementation (wl_cfg80211_sched_scan_start/stop and
wl_notify_sched_scan_results on top of the firmware PFN, dhd_pno.c), but
it is compiled only with WL_SCHED_SCAN, which the Makefile never sets.
The wiphy then lacks WIPHY_FLAG_SUPPORTS_SCHED_SCAN and reports
max_sched_scan_ssids = max_match_sets = 0, and nl80211 answers every
START_SCHED_SCAN with EOPNOTSUPP. PNO was left reachable only through the
Android private command PNOSETUP, which nothing sends since wificond.

Add CONFIG_BCMDHD_SCHED_SCAN (default n) that sets WL_SCHED_SCAN. With it
the driver advertises 16 sched-scan SSIDs and match sets and runs the
request as a legacy PFN scan: 30 s for 4 scans, then backing off to
120 s (PNO_TIME, PNO_REPEAT, PNO_FREQ_EXPO_MAX in wl_cfg80211.c), all in
firmware. A PFN_NET_FOUND event wakes the host (10 s wake lock,
CUSTOM_PNO_EVENT_LOCK_xTIME), the driver runs a targeted escan and
reports cfg80211_sched_scan_results(), and the framework connects.

wificond always puts the wildcard SSID into NL80211_ATTR_SCAN_SSIDS, so
the driver's n_ssids != 0 check is met without hidden networks.
Syntax-checked with the build's own gcc 4.9 command line for
wl_cfg80211.c and wl_android.c: no new warnings.

Observed on the SM-T815 (build 21, 2026-11-22/23): Wi-Fi dropped with the
screen off (AP deauth reason 7) and stayed down until the screen came on,
up to 20.8 h; numPnoScanAttempts=0. Analysis: staging/wifi-pno/.
---
index c8b9d7d..e1d13cb 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/bcmdhd4358a3/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/bcmdhd4358a3/Kconfig
@@ -129,6 +129,19 @@ config BCMDHD_PCIE
 	---help---
 	  Enable PCI Express I/F Support
 
+config BCMDHD_SCHED_SCAN
+	bool "PNO through cfg80211 scheduled scan"
+	depends on (BCM4354 || BCM4358)
+	default n
+	---help---
+	  Build the driver with WL_SCHED_SCAN: advertise nl80211 scheduled
+	  scan (WIPHY_FLAG_SUPPORTS_SCHED_SCAN, max_sched_scan_ssids,
+	  max_match_sets) and run NL80211_CMD_START_SCHED_SCAN as a firmware
+	  PFN (preferred network offload) scan. wificond starts such a scan
+	  for the Wi-Fi framework while the screen is off and Wi-Fi is
+	  disconnected. Without it the driver keeps PNO only behind the
+	  Android private command PNOSETUP, which nothing uses any more.
+
 config BCMDHD_DEBUG_PAGEALLOC
 	bool "Enable Memory Pagealloc Debugging Support"
 	depends on (BCM4354 || BCM4358)
diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/bcmdhd4358a3/Makefile b/drivers/net/wireless/bcmdhd4358a3/Makefile
index def2d46..778844a 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/bcmdhd4358a3/Makefile
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/bcmdhd4358a3/Makefile
@@ -68,6 +68,11 @@ endif
 DHDCFLAGS += -DCUSTOMER_HW4
 DHDCFLAGS += -DWL_CFG80211
 
+# Scheduled scan (PNO) for wificond, see CONFIG_BCMDHD_SCHED_SCAN
+ifeq ($(CONFIG_BCMDHD_SCHED_SCAN),y)
+DHDCFLAGS += -DWL_SCHED_SCAN
+endif
+
 # DMA64 suppports on 64bit Architecture
 ifeq ($(CONFIG_64BIT),y)
 DHDCFLAGS := $(filter-out -DBCMDMA32,$(DHDCFLAGS))
